drm/asahi: flush stamps on the last render and compute command again

submit() counts the commands twice: first to find the last render and the
last compute command, then to submit them with flush_stamps set on those.
Since the UAPI rework the first pass stores a render's index in last_compute
and a compute's in last_render, so no command ever matches and flush_stamps
is never set. Up to asahi-6.12 it was set on the last command of each kind.
Reported as AsahiLinux/linux#633.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/queue/mod.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/queue/mod.rs
index 594b271..f410191 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/queue/mod.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/queue/mod.rs
@@ -719,11 +719,11 @@ fn submit<'drm>(
 
             match header.cmd_type as u32 {
                 uapi::drm_asahi_cmd_type_DRM_ASAHI_CMD_RENDER => {
-                    last_compute = nr_commands;
+                    last_render = nr_commands;
                     nr_render += 1;
                 }
                 uapi::drm_asahi_cmd_type_DRM_ASAHI_CMD_COMPUTE => {
-                    last_render = nr_commands;
+                    last_compute = nr_commands;
                     nr_compute += 1;
                 }
                 _ => {}
